{"reference":"Acts 6","book":"Acts","chapter":6,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Stephen’s Speech in Context","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The accusations and council scene at the end of this chapter lead into Stephen’s speech in the next chapter. That speech retells contested moments in Israel’s history as rhetoric directed toward hostile council members; it should not be read as assigning blanket blame to all Jews. Some early textual witnesses preserve a substantially distinctive form of Acts, so individual differences in wording need to be considered case by case.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_acts_006_50bd4a618316bd25ccadbc6f"]}]}],"generated_metadata":null}